{"audio":{"src":"https://pub-13abeb101e2945d2a7f60234f6faf52e.r2.dev/materials/a2-lithuania-famous-places-food/audio/main-b6f920a26a8b.mp3","durationSec":324.6,"cues":[{"start":0,"end":2.82,"text":"Your trip starts in Vilnius, the capital of Lithuania."},{"start":3.48,"end":4.8,"text":"You walk through the Old Town."},{"start":5.36,"end":8.54,"text":"The streets are small, and there are old churches everywhere."},{"start":9.24,"end":12.42,"text":"This Old Town is very old, and it is also very big."},{"start":12.92,"end":16.08,"text":"Many of its buildings and streets are hundreds of years old."},{"start":16.62,"end":20.02,"text":"Because of this, UNESCO put it on its World Heritage list."},{"start":20.72,"end":23.96,"text":"UNESCO is a world group that takes care of very important places."},{"start":24.88,"end":29.68,"text":"At lunch, you go into Etno Dvaras, a restaurant with food from Lithuania."},{"start":30.52,"end":33.68,"text":"You order cepelinai, the national dish of Lithuania."},{"start":33.68,"end":37.3,"text":"Cepelinai are big potato dumplings."},{"start":38.22,"end":41.88,"text":"A dumpling is a soft ball of food with more food inside."},{"start":42.56,"end":47.7,"text":"Inside cepelinai, there is usually meat or curd cheese, a soft white cheese."},{"start":48.44,"end":52.62,"text":"On top, there is a sauce of sour cream with small pieces of bacon."},{"start":53.3,"end":54.28,"text":"Why the funny name?"},{"start":54.58,"end":57.88,"text":"A zeppelin is a long, round flying ship."},{"start":58.32,"end":59.94,"text":"It carries people, like a plane."},{"start":59.94,"end":63,"text":"Cepelinai have the same long, round shape."},{"start":63.9,"end":65.64,"text":"So people named them after the zeppelin."},{"start":66.36,"end":72,"text":"At Etno Dvaras, one plate of cepelinai costs 9.55 euros."},{"start":72,"end":75.17,"text":"The next day, you take a train from Vilnius to Trakai."},{"start":75.17,"end":78.86,"text":"Trakai Island Castle stands on a small island in a lake."},{"start":79.5,"end":80.9,"text":"You walk to it over a bridge."},{"start":81.48,"end":84.74,"text":"The castle is red and more than 600 years old."},{"start":85.58,"end":88.12,"text":"Inside, there is a museum about the history of Lithuania."},{"start":89.12,"end":93.03,"text":"After the castle, you go to Karaimų Street to try kibinai."},{"start":93.03,"end":95,"text":"Kibinai are small pastries."},{"start":96.1,"end":97.72,"text":"Inside, there is meat and onion."},{"start":98.38,"end":101.62,"text":"The traditional meat is mutton, the meat of an adult sheep."},{"start":101.62,"end":104.4,"text":"Kibinai are the food of the Karaim people."},{"start":105.1,"end":108.56,"text":"In English, Karaimų Street is Street of the Karaim."},{"start":109.12,"end":110.04,"text":"Who are the Karaim?"},{"start":110.9,"end":114.68,"text":"More than 600 years ago, Vytautas was the ruler of Lithuania."},{"start":115.32,"end":119.88,"text":"He brought Karaim families to Trakai from Crimea, a place far in the south."},{"start":120.7,"end":122.78,"text":"Their job was to keep his castle safe."},{"start":122.78,"end":126.48,"text":"Vytautas gave them land here, and they lived on this street."},{"start":127.32,"end":128.92,"text":"That is why the street has their name."},{"start":129.54,"end":133.02,"text":"They brought their own food with them, and kibinai were part of it."},{"start":133.6,"end":136.9,"text":"A small group of Karaim people still lives in Trakai today."},{"start":137.74,"end":141.9,"text":"On day three, you go north to the city of Šiauliai."},{"start":141.9,"end":144.6,"text":"The Hill of Crosses is a short drive from the city."},{"start":145.34,"end":147.96,"text":"From far away, it looks like a small hill."},{"start":148.98,"end":153.94,"text":"Up close, you see crosses everywhere, big and small, wooden and metal."},{"start":154.9,"end":158.64,"text":"Today, there are more than 100,000 crosses on the hill."},{"start":159.58,"end":160.24,"text":"Why are they here?"},{"start":160.96,"end":164.82,"text":"In the 1800s, many people in Lithuania died in fights against Russia."},{"start":165.22,"end":166.78,"text":"They wanted their country to be free."},{"start":167.54,"end":169.06,"text":"Their families never found the bodies."},{"start":169.58,"end":172.34,"text":"So the families had no place to visit and remember them."},{"start":173.3,"end":175.18,"text":"Instead, they put crosses on this hill."},{"start":176.4,"end":178.78,"text":"Later, Lithuania was part of the Soviet Union."},{"start":179.56,"end":181.92,"text":"The Soviet leaders did not want people to pray."},{"start":182.46,"end":184.02,"text":"So they did not want the crosses."},{"start":185.2,"end":188,"text":"Again and again, they destroyed the crosses on the hill."},{"start":188.88,"end":193.6,"text":"The first time, in 1961, they destroyed all the crosses in one day."},{"start":194.54,"end":198.02,"text":"Crosses on the hill were against the law, and people were punished for them."},{"start":198.4,"end":200.86,"text":"But people came back at night and put up new crosses."},{"start":201.88,"end":205.14,"text":"In the dark, it was harder to see them, but it was still dangerous."},{"start":205.8,"end":206.54,"text":"They came anyway."},{"start":207.54,"end":210.52,"text":"So the hill became a sign that the people did not give up."},{"start":211.8,"end":214.9,"text":"After your visit, you eat lunch in Šiauliai."},{"start":214.9,"end":218.86,"text":"It is a hot July day, so you order šaltibarščiai."},{"start":218.86,"end":220.72,"text":"This is a famous cold pink soup."},{"start":221.06,"end":223.42,"text":"It is made with beetroot and kefir."},{"start":223.82,"end":227.3,"text":"Beetroot is a dark red vegetable, and it makes the soup pink."},{"start":228,"end":230.58,"text":"Kefir is a thick milk drink, a little like yogurt."},{"start":231.3,"end":235.42,"text":"People eat this soup on hot summer days, with boiled potatoes on the side."},{"start":236.58,"end":238.62,"text":"Your last stop is the Curonian Spit."},{"start":239.4,"end":242.56,"text":"A spit is a long, thin piece of land in the sea."},{"start":243.24,"end":245.26,"text":"On one side is the Baltic Sea."},{"start":245.74,"end":247.5,"text":"On the other is the Curonian Lagoon."},{"start":248.14,"end":251.48,"text":"A lagoon is a big, quiet area of water next to the sea."},{"start":252,"end":253.1,"text":"There is land in between."},{"start":253.64,"end":256.78,"text":"To get there, you take a short ferry from the city of Klaipėda."},{"start":256.78,"end":259.12,"text":"It goes to Smiltynė, at the north end of the spit."},{"start":259.62,"end":260.96,"text":"Then you take a bus to Nida."},{"start":261.38,"end":262.58,"text":"The ride is about one hour."},{"start":263.42,"end":266.32,"text":"In the village of Nida, you climb the Parnidis Dune."},{"start":266.96,"end":269.64,"text":"A dune is a hill of sand that the wind makes."},{"start":270.22,"end":271.56,"text":"It is 52 metres high."},{"start":272.16,"end":275.56,"text":"From the top, you see sand, forest and water on both sides."},{"start":276.16,"end":279.68,"text":"In the 1800s, fishing was the most important work in Nida."},{"start":280.3,"end":281.82,"text":"People caught fish in the lagoon."},{"start":282.24,"end":284.7,"text":"But there were no fridges then, and fish goes bad fast."},{"start":285.38,"end":287.08,"text":"So they smoked the fish over a fire."},{"start":287.76,"end":290.56,"text":"Smoke dries the fish, so it stays OK to eat for longer."},{"start":291.28,"end":293,"text":"They often used the wood of the alder tree."},{"start":293.38,"end":297.24,"text":"Its smoke is soft and sweet, and it makes the fish golden."},{"start":298.12,"end":301.38,"text":"Today, small shops all over the spit sell smoked fish."},{"start":302.18,"end":305.8,"text":"In Nida, you go to a café called Tik pas Joną."},{"start":305.8,"end":308.82,"text":"In English, the name is Only at Jonas's Place."},{"start":309.7,"end":311.58,"text":"This café smokes its own fish."},{"start":312.52,"end":316,"text":"You choose bream, a fish from the lagoon, or eel."},{"start":316.96,"end":319.72,"text":"An eel is a long fish that looks like a snake."},{"start":320.4,"end":324,"text":"The fish is still warm, and you eat it with bread and your hands."}],"words":[{"text":"Your","start":0,"end":0.2},{"text":"trip","start":0.2,"end":0.4},{"text":"starts","start":0.4,"end":0.78},{"text":"in","start":0.78,"end":1.06},{"text":"Vilnius","start":1.06,"end":1.5},{"text":"the","start":1.84,"end":1.94},{"text":"capital","start":1.94,"end":2.26},{"text":"of","start":2.26,"end":2.5},{"text":"Lithuania","start":2.5,"end":2.82},{"text":"You","start":3.48,"end":3.68},{"text":"walk","start":3.68,"end":3.9},{"text":"through","start":3.9,"end":4.12},{"text":"the","start":4.12,"end":4.26},{"text":"Old","start":4.26,"end":4.46},{"text":"Town","start":4.46,"end":4.8},{"text":"The","start":5.36,"end":5.48},{"text":"streets","start":5.48,"end":5.76},{"text":"are","start":5.76,"end":5.96},{"text":"small","start":5.96,"end":6.36},{"text":"and","start":6.7,"end":6.86},{"text":"there","start":6.86,"end":6.98},{"text":"are","start":6.98,"end":7.14},{"text":"old","start":7.14,"end":7.48},{"text":"churches","start":7.48,"end":7.96},{"text":"everywhere","start":7.96,"end":8.54},{"text":"This","start":9.24,"end":9.42},{"text":"Old","start":9.42,"end":9.62},{"text":"Town","start":9.62,"end":9.9},{"text":"is","start":9.9,"end":10.14},{"text":"very","start":10.14,"end":10.42},{"text":"old","start":10.42,"end":10.8},{"text":"and","start":11.08,"end":11.24},{"text":"it","start":11.24,"end":11.34},{"text":"is","start":11.34,"end":11.46},{"text":"also","start":11.46,"end":11.8},{"text":"very","start":11.8,"end":12.06},{"text":"big","start":12.06,"end":12.42},{"text":"Many","start":12.92,"end":13.08},{"text":"of","start":13.08,"end":13.22},{"text":"its","start":13.22,"end":13.38},{"text":"buildings","start":13.38,"end":13.76},{"tex